        "title": "The Byzantine Empire - Eastern Rome, 330–1453",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nTHE CONTINUITY ARGUMENT:\nRoman Empire (27 BCE)\n       ↓\nTetrarchy (3rd century)\n       ↓\nConstantine moves capital to Constantinople (330 CE)\n       ↓\nWestern Empire \"falls\" 476 CE — but the Eastern half\ncontinues unbroken. From Constantinople's perspective:\nRome fell; we did not. We ARE Rome.\n       ↓\nByzantine Empire (the Eastern Roman Empire)\ncontinues until 1453 CE\nTOTAL DURATION: ~1,123 years from Constantine, ~1,480 from Augustus\n```"
    }
